    {
      "block_id": 15,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "(Not a mirror— interrupt occurs when the buffer \nbecomes empty.) When bit 14 is a 1, the data in the output \ndata register (SERDAT) has been transferred to the serial \noutput shift register, so SERDAT is ready to accept another \noutput word. This is also true when the buffer is empty.\n",
      "bbox": [
        226.92262268066406,
        358.85107421875,
        489.9685363769531,
        420.944091796875
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
